pietro bocelli is a 27 year old who has  a phd in mechanical engineering  while he was teaching a course a student  discovered that he's also a model  this got picked up in the western media  and he's quickly dubbed the world's  hottest math teacher  alex bellows at the guardian recently  interviewed pietro  two of the questions i found interesting  were he asked whether pietro knew any  mathematical party tricks and whether he  could calculate 43 by 67 in his head  it turned out he didn't know any tricks  and that's a shame  so in this video i'm going to teach you  how you can do 43 by 67 in your head  using some of the methods i've already  taught  the first method  is a video i made about how you can  multiply two numbers that are close to  each other  the procedure is to look at the average  of the two numbers and square it and  subtract the difference from the average  and square that  43 and 67 have an average of 55 and both  numbers have a difference of 12 from 55  so we can compute the product as 55  squared minus 12 squared  now we know 12 squared is 144  but what's 55 squared  in another method i've taught you can  square numbers in the 50s very easily  the method is to add  the difference from 50 to 25 that  becomes the leading digits of your  answer  and then the last two digits are the  square of the difference from 50.  55 has a difference of 5 from 50  so 25 plus 5 is 30 and 5 squared is 25  therefore 55 squared is 30 25.  there is another method you could use  you can also square a number ending in  five what you do is you look at the tens  digit and you multiply it by one more  than itself  you then append 25 at the end of the  number  here the tens digit is 5  so 5 times 6 is 30  we then append 25 to get 55 squared is  30 25.  putting it all together we have 43 times  67 is 55 squared minus 12 squared  which is then 30 25 minus 144  which we can then come to 28.81  so while each of these tricks i've  taught you may have seemed like it was  solving 